{"id": "EUVD-2026-99007", "enisaUuid": "322e535f-4e90-3d96-877d-0305a19e935e", "description": "Razorpay IFSC Ruby gem through 2.0.62 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows attackers to redirect API requests by supplying a crafted IFSC code to IFSC.find or IFSC#get. Attackers can submit network-path references or absolute URIs that URI.join resolves as a new host, sending GET requests to internal or attacker-chosen hosts and returning parsed response fields.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:22:04", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/rJYWKMsiMg", "https://github.com/razorpay/ifsc/blob/v2.0.62/src/ruby/ifsc.rb#L53-L58", "https://github.com/razorpay/ifsc", "https://rubygems.org/gems/ifsc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/razorpay-ifsc-ruby-gem-through-2.0.62-ssrf-via-ifsc-lookup"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110222", "GHSA-crh7-6qx8-9v9q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7998a118-fa86-3106-a2a0-a8cf01209f0f", "product": {"name": "IFSC", "vendor": {"name": "razorpay"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.62"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "831cbd5b-a3df-3445-ad58-24e732569db9", "vendor": {"name": "razorpay"}}], "isExploited": false}